+; The yuvShader with Y read through a Catmull-Rom (bicubic) filter: the 4x4
+; texels around the point, in 9 bilinear reads (the middle two of each row and
+; column read as one, at the point between them their weights give). U and V
+; stay bilinear. The sampler has to filter linearly.
+;
+; Per axis, the x one in .x and the y one in .y (texel i's center at i + 0.5):
+;   b = floor(uv * size - 0.5): the texel whose center is at or before the point
+;   f = how far past that center the point is, 0..1
+;   weights of texels b - 1 .. b + 2:
+;     w0 = f * (-0.5 + f * (1 - 0.5 f))
+;     w1 = 1 + f^2 * (-2.5 + 1.5 f)
+;     w2 = f * (0.5 + f * (2 - 1.5 f))
+;     w3 = f^2 * (-0.5 + 0.5 f)
+;   read at (then divided by size):
+;     c0 = b - 0.5, c12 = b + 0.5 + w2 / (w1 + w2), c3 = b + 2.5
+; R2.xy = b, R3 = (f, f^2), R4 = (w0, w2), R5 = (w3, w1 + w2);
+; coordinates R6 = (c0, c3), R9 = (c12, c0 y, c3 y), R10 = (c0 x, c12 y, c3 x);
+; columns c0, c12, c3 of Y read into R13, R14, R15, rows c0, c12, c3 in .x, .y,
+; .z; U in R17.y, V in R17.z.
+;
+; No two operands of a group read different GPRs through the same channel in
+; the same cycle (src0, src1, src2 go in cycles 0, 1, 2; PV, PS, constants
+; and literals don't count), each group reads one constant register and has at
+; most 4 literals (the assembler gives every one its own).
